      "correction_id": "LEAD-RITUAL-01",
      "found_by": "lead adversarial test, owner attack list section 13",
      "defect": "27 rows asserted rite membership where the only rite named is a category term: 24 on YAJNA-SACRIFICE and 3 on bare ISTI. A mantra that names 'sacrifice' is not thereby a member of a specific rite.",
      "fix": "Retyped to NAMES_RITE_CATEGORY_GENERICALLY and downgraded to PROBABLE, so the validator treats them as staged and not importable. Prior row_kind preserved on each row.",
      "value_space_enumerated": "All 45 rite keys were listed before choosing these two, rather than grepping for the term the lead expected. The other 43 are genuine named rites -- agnihotra, agnistoma, asvamedha, darsapurnamasa, rajasuya, vajapeya, upanayana and so on.",
      "deliberately_not_retyped": "SOMA-PRESSING, 22 rows. It is a ritual act rather than a named rite, which is a different objection from being a category: soma pressing occurs inside many rites, so a mantra naming it has named something specific. Referred to the owner rather than swept in.",
      "unchanged_and_verified_clean": "The core boundary: 0 of 3,045 rows keyed outside the four recensions, and evidence_source_type still distinguishes SRAUTASUTRA 1,303 / BRAHMANA 992 / GRHYASUTRA 527 / SAMHITA 223."
